RideDash is an independent, brand-neutral motorcycle navigation and ride companion project.

The compatible-display interoperability layer is based on publicly available interoperability research and clean-room reimplementation using public iOS APIs. The project does not include manufacturer firmware, private keys, proprietary certificates, extracted assets, or safety-critical vehicle-control functionality.

Some protocol behavior and packet sequencing were informed by publicly available open-source projects and research notes, including OpenDash / better-dash style motorcycle display interoperability work. Review and preserve the license notices of any third-party source code that is directly incorporated in future changes.

Royal Enfield, Tripper, and any other third-party product or company names are trademarks of their respective owners. RideDash is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by those trademark owners.

The project permanently excludes ECU, throttle, brakes, ABS, traction control, immobilizer, firmware modification, engine control, and other safety-critical vehicle command paths.
